melody:
# Chorus (as published by Remick, 1912)
We were sail-ing a-long On Moon-light Bay,
Bb4/. C5// D5/. C#5// D5 F4(4) ~F4 F#4 G4/ Eb5. D5(4) ~D5
We could hear the voic-es ring-ing, They seemed to say,
D5/. C#5// D5/. C#5// D5/. Eb5// D5(2) C5(2) ~C5 B4 C5 D5 F4(4) ~F4
"You have stol-en her heart, Now don't go 'way!"
Bb4/. C5// D5/. C#5// D5 F4(4) ~F4 F#4 G4/ Eb5. D5(4) ~D5(2)
As we sang Love's Old Sweet Song On Moon-light Bay.
Eb5 D5 C5 F4 C5 F4 C5 F4 C5/ D5. Bb4(4) ~Bb4

# Once more
We were sail-ing a-long On Moon-light Bay,
Bb4/. C5// D5/. C#5// D5 F4(4) ~F4 F#4 G4/ Eb5. D5(4) ~D5
We could hear the voic-es ring-ing, They seemed to say,
D5/. C#5// D5/. C#5// D5/. Eb5// D5(2) C5(2) ~C5 B4 C5 D5 F4(4) ~F4
"You have stol-en her heart, Now don't go 'way!"
Bb4/. C5// D5/. C#5// D5 F4(4) ~F4 F#4 G4/ Eb5. D5(4) ~D5(2)
As we sang Love's Old Sweet Song On Moon-light Bay.
Eb5 D5 C5 F4 C5 F4 C5 F4 C5/ D5. Bb4(4) ~Bb4(2) r(2)
